.TH CLOPS_TRIPDEBUG 1 "May 2026" "v2.0.1a" "CamClops - Trip Detection Debugger"
.SH NAME
clops_tripdebug \- trip detection debugger for CamClops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_tripdebug
.RB [ \-T | \-f ]
.I path_to_dashcam_folder
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_tripdebug
runs CamClops trip detection directly against a dashcam footage directory and
displays the results without reading or writing any manifest.  It is a
diagnostic tool for verifying that footage is being grouped into trips as
expected.
.PP
Trip detection uses the active camera profile
.RI ( activeProfileId
in
.IR ~/.config/camclops/camclops.json )
to determine directory layout, filename patterns, and segment duration.
Run
.BR "clops_probe \-\-wizard" " " PATH
to create a profile for cameras other than the built-in Pruveeo D90.
.PP
Without options,
.B clops_tripdebug
prints a summary table of detected trips.  Use
.B \-T
for a full segment listing or
.B \-f
for an interactive drill-down.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-T ", " \-\-tree
Print the complete segment tree for every detected trip and exit.  Each
segment shows its timestamp and which cameras (Front/Rear/Left/Right) have
footage files present.
.TP
.B \-f ", " \-\-full
Interactive mode.  Displays the summary list, then prompts for a trip ID to
inspect.  Enter a numeric ID to see its segment tree.  Enter
.B R
to redraw the summary,
.B Q
to quit.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the CamClops version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Summary (default)
.nf
  ID    Start Timestamp      Duration        Segments
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
  1     2026-02-09 04:38:38  1h 22m 14s      83
  2     2026-02-09 08:14:01  0h 34m 07s      35

2 trip(s) detected.
.fi
.SS Tree (\-T or \-f drill-down)
.nf
Trip #1  [2026-02-09  04:38:38]  duration=1h 22m 14s  segments=83
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  [  1]  20260209_043838  [F.L.]
         F: 20260209_043838F.ts
         L: 20260209_043838L.ts
  [  2]  20260209_043938  [FBLR]
  ...
.fi
